{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"QBusiness: New-QBUSApplication Cmdlet | AWS Tools for PowerShell","context":"## Description\n\nCreates an Amazon Q Business application.\nThere are new tiers for Amazon Q Business. Not all features in Amazon Q Business Pro are also available in Amazon Q Business Lite. For information on what's included in Amazon Q Business Lite and what's included in Amazon Q Business Pro, see Amazon Q Business tiers. You must use the Amazon Q Business console to assign subscription tiers to users.\nAn Amazon Q Apps service linked role will be created if it's absent in the Amazon Web Services account when QAppsConfiguration is enabled in the request. For more information, see Using service-linked roles for Q Apps.\nWhen you create an application, Amazon Q Business may securely transmit data for processing from your selected Amazon Web Services region, but within your geography. For more information, see Cross region inference in Amazon Q Business","url":"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/powershell/v4/reference/index.html?page=New-QBUSApplication.html&tocid=New-QBUSApplication"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"create-application — AWS CLI 2.39.2 Command Reference","context":"## Description\n\nCreates an Amazon Q Business application.\n\n### Note\n\nThere are new tiers for Amazon Q Business. Not all features in Amazon Q Business Pro are also available in Amazon Q Business Lite. For information on what’s included in Amazon Q Business Lite and what’s included in Amazon Q Business Pro, see Amazon Q Business tiers . You must use the Amazon Q Business console to assign subscription tiers to users.\n\nAn Amazon Q Apps service linked role will be created if it’s absent in the Amazon Web Services account when `QAppsConfiguration` is enabled in the request. For more information, see Using service-linked roles for Q Apps .\n\nWhen you create an application, Amazon Q Business may securely transmit data for processing from your selected Amazon Web Services region, but within your geography. For more information, see Cross region inference in Amazon Q Business .\n\nSee also: AWS API Documentation","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/qbusiness/create-application.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"create-application — AWS CLI 1.46.2 Command Reference","context":"## Description\n\nCreates an Amazon Q Business application.\n\n### Note\n\nThere are new tiers for Amazon Q Business. Not all features in Amazon Q Business Pro are also available in Amazon Q Business Lite. For information on what’s included in Amazon Q Business Lite and what’s included in Amazon Q Business Pro, see Amazon Q Business tiers . You must use the Amazon Q Business console to assign subscription tiers to users.\n\nAn Amazon Q Apps service linked role will be created if it’s absent in the Amazon Web Services account when `QAppsConfiguration` is enabled in the request. For more information, see Using service-linked roles for Q Apps .\n\nWhen you create an application, Amazon Q Business may securely transmit data for processing from your selected Amazon Web Services region, but within your geography. For more information, see Cross region inference in Amazon Q Business .\n\nSee also: AWS API Documentation","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/v1/reference/qbusiness/create-application.html"}]}}

